     {
      "id": "6afac381475485d832347688",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Reconciliation Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is reconciliation automation?\", \"a\": \"Reconciliation automation is software that pairs two sets of records, such as bank lines and ledger entries, under a rule you set. AccountingTools defines the manual task: \\\"A reconciliation involves matching two sets of records to see if there are any differences.\\\" The automated version runs that check on new lines and leaves a person the differences.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up reconciliation automation?\", \"a\": \"Describe the reconciliation in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>: the two records, the match rule, and who reviews the leftovers. Emergent builds the app from that prompt, and the app connects to your ledger and bank feed through their APIs. Test it on a month your team already closed before it runs on the current one.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does bank reconciliation automation still leave for a person to do?\", \"a\": \"It leaves every line that matches no ledger entry, and a person decides what each one is. AccountingTools says a bank reconciliation compares \\\"cash records with the bank statement, identifying deposits in transit, outstanding checks, fees, and errors.\\\" The rule pairs the clean lines, while naming an error or recording a fee stays with your accountant.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which accounts should reconciliation automation cover first?\", \"a\": \"Start with the one that has the most lines each month, because that is where a match rule saves the most hours. For a business with one busy checking account, that is the bank reconciliation. Payouts and supplier statements can follow once it runs clean, and the jobs around them, such as bill approvals, belong to <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/finance'>finance automation</a> more broadly.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does reconciliation automation handle deposits in transit?\", \"a\": \"Leave them open on the ledger side until the bank line arrives and pairs with them. Sage defines the term: \\\"Deposits in transit are deposits you have recorded in your accounting system before they are cleared by the bank.\\\" Set a number of days after which a deposit still waiting goes to a person.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can reconciliation automation allow small differences in amount or date?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if you write the tolerance into the rule, such as amounts within $1.00 or dates up to 3 days apart. Keep the tolerance tight for the first month. Widen it only where the test month shows that a near miss was a true match every time.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should reconciliation automation run?\", \"a\": \"Run each reconciliation as often as its records arrive: daily for bank lines and cash deposits, on each payout for a card processor, and monthly for supplier statements. A daily run keeps the review queue to a few lines instead of a month of them at close. Apps built on Emergent carry no task cap, which leaves room for a daily run on every account.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one reconciliation automation cover several bank accounts?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Connect each account's feed to the same app and give each account its own rule, since a payroll account and a card account clear in different ways. The review queue can show every account together or one at a time. Every match, from all the accounts, stays in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does reconciliation automation handle one deposit that pays several invoices?\", \"a\": \"The rule groups them: it adds open invoices from the same customer until their total equals the deposit, then records one deposit against all of them. A deposit that no group of invoices adds up to goes to the review queue with the closest combinations beside it. On paid plans, the grouping rule sits in the code Emergent exports to your GitHub repository.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can reconciliation automation check carrier invoices against loads?\", \"a\": \"Yes: a rule can compare each carrier invoice with the rate agreed on its load and send any invoice over that rate to a person. The invoice is read into fields the same way a supplier statement is. For the load side of that work, booking and tracking, see <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/freight-broker'>freight broker automation</a>.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ad21d95eef2cea1194f0017",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Recruitment Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are the 7 steps of the recruitment process?\", \"a\": \"One common list has seven steps: identify the hiring need, create the job description, source candidates, screen and shortlist them, conduct interviews, make the offer, and onboard the new hire. Start recruitment automation with screening and the hand-offs between stages, since those repeat the same way for every candidate.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up recruitment automation?\", \"a\": \"Pick the hiring step that costs your team the most time, such as applications nobody reads for a week, and describe the rule that fixes it to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a> in plain English. Emergent builds the app and its database from that prompt. Add the next rule by prompting once the first one runs cleanly on real applicants.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the 5 steps of the recruitment process?\", \"a\": \"A five-step version folds interviews into screening: identify the hiring need, write a detailed job description, source candidates, screen applicants with resume reviews and interviews, then hold final interviews, check references, and extend the offer. Next to the seven-step list, it leaves out onboarding and treats the offer as part of the final decision.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I post new openings to social channels as part of a recruiting workflow?\", \"a\": \"Trigger the post from the job record. When a requisition is approved, the app drafts a post with the title and apply link, and a recruiter approves the wording before it goes out. The scheduling and approval steps are the same ones <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/social-media'>social media automation</a> uses for marketing posts, with the job record as the source.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which decisions in a hiring workflow should stay with a person?\", \"a\": \"Every decision about a specific candidate: who advances after an interview, who gets an offer, and any rejection that is not a plain fail on a hard requirement. Automate the routing and reminders around those calls. Log who made each decision and the date, for the day a candidate asks.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is recruitment automation?\", \"a\": \"Recruitment automation is software that handles the repeatable parts of hiring on rules you set: sorting applications against fixed requirements, reminding the person who owns a stage, and checking each offer against its pay band. Your team still interviews the candidates and decides who gets hired.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can recruitment automation handle job requisition approvals?\", \"a\": \"Route each new requisition through an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/approval-workflow'>approval workflow</a> before the job is posted. The hiring manager submits the role and its budgeted pay, and HR or finance approves it or sends it back with a note. Only an approved requisition can be posted, and the approver's name and date stay on the record.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I automate first in recruitment?\", \"a\": \"Automate the stage where candidates wait longest, not the busiest one. Pull the last 3 months of stage dates from your applicant tracking system and compare the median wait at each step. A time limit and a reminder on that one stage save the most days. Emergent builds a first app for it from a prompt, and the free tier covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I measure whether recruitment automation is working?\", \"a\": \"Compare the days candidates spend in each stage, and the number who withdraw, for the month before launch and each month after. Also count how many knockout declines a recruiter overturns: a rising count means a question is too strict. Apps built with Emergent can show these numbers on a live dashboard.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can recruitment automation create invoices after an agency placement?\", \"a\": \"Yes: trigger the invoice from the placement record. When a candidate's start date is confirmed, the app creates the invoice with the agreed fee and emails it to the client contact. Chasing unpaid invoices is the job of <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/accounts-receivable'>accounts receivable automation</a>. Apps built with Emergent connect to your accounting software through its API.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
